    {
      "id": "56f467d14837e75b70ee1374e3abae36328b8f57",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2916538872,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have a few concerns about some edge cases that it will take me a bit to write up. As a quick note, it looks to me like certain illegal sequences are not getting any sort of display (middle dot or otherwise.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-26T19:09:30.802Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-27T02:46:19.567Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434636192,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22398,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2916997545,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@johnthacker What I can tell for now(not an unicode expert):\n\n1. zero(e.g. `U+200C`, `U+200D`) or tiny(e.g. `U+202F`) width spaces or separators\n2. combining marks(e.g. accent `U+0301`) that\n   1. appears alone, like when interpreting tcp timestamp option hex value as UTF8.\n   2. cross line, e.g. `A\\u0301` is split into two lines, and combining mark is invisible on its own.\n3. other `!isprint` or `iscntl` characters are already excluded.\n\nSo we need to decide how to display these characters.\n1. For zero or tiny width spaces, I think it might be better to show \"dot\".\n2. For combining marks, there might be several choices.\n   1. one way is to treat them all as \"dot\", but that might hurt the display of normal combinations on the same line (e.g. `61 cc 81` displayed as `a..`)\n   2. the other way is to print them normally if they followed a printable character(e.g. `61 cc 81` displayed as `Á`), but this way we need to display\n   3. print a white space before every combining mark. but that may (e.g. `61 cc 81` displayed as `a ́`.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5791322,
            "username": "lotabout",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jinzhou Zhang",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fae1714fe386c818c4d564840304aecda773e63bbdce1dcb24e7da625eba574b?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/lotabout"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-27T02:46:19.269Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-27T02:46:19.269Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 434636192,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 22398,
          "commands_changes": {}
