    {
      "id": "26fe3a3bbb15f6280b2e48831e127eea6bf20627",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2917021784,
          "type": null,
          "body": "[ping_man_shrugging.pcapng](/uploads/4109c09283c12539262e56d6f96e7c2e/ping_man_shrugging.pcapng)\n\nOnly allowing printable characters (BTW, the `!g_unichar_iscntrl(uc)` is redundant, since `g_unichar_isprint()` already excluded them) does keep us from seeing \"man shrugging\" instead of \"person shrugging\" because it officially uses a zero-width joiner, like other emoji combinations:\n\nFrame 1: ![image](/uploads/820eff3e25b5b4e495426bcd2d49e583/image.png){width=702 height=97}\n\nFrame 3: ![image](/uploads/4af26f2a8bb78cea92856acdba1dcda0/image.png){width=702 height=97}\n\nSelection box is a little weird around the masculine symbol (the next character is a \"selection\" character):\n![image](/uploads/2cbda6aae96ba7cf3f53d5d40d2738b3/image.png){width=702 height=97}\n\nEdited your code to get this for frame 3 so the ZWJ isn't excluded from processing:\n\n![image](/uploads/7535744bf599c5f72ddf10e24517999d/image.png){width=702 height=97}\n\nBut it gets a little weird when the emoji is split across lines in frame 1:\n![image](/uploads/89a169574cad9d029a5e59ac8d943562/image.png){width=702 height=97}",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-11-27T03:17:28.320Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-11-27T03:19:10.266Z",
